A bank transfer

The `Mobile app` calls the `Transfer API`. The `Transfer API` checks the
`Fraud check` and writes to the `Ledger`. The `Ledger` sends money through the
`Payment rail`. The `Mobile app` must never call the `Ledger`, with the reason
`audit`. The team `Payments` owns the `Transfer API` and the `Ledger`. The team
`Risk` owns the `Fraud check`. Use the key `owner`. Write the story `transfer`
for the four steps in order and show it as a sequence.
---
Transfer API, Ledger { owner: Payments }
Fraud check { owner: Risk }
story transfer {
  Mobile app -> Transfer API: transfer
  Transfer API -> Fraud check: check
  Transfer API -> Ledger: write
  Ledger -> Payment rail: send money
}
Mobile app -x Ledger: audit
show sequence of transfer
